# Copy to .env.local for local work. On Vercel, set these under
# Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Only THREE variables belong in this repository. Everything else — the
# database, the encryption keys, the Cloudinary secret, the Resend key — is
# backend-only and lives in Railway. Nothing here may hold a value that would
# be damaging to read, because anything in a Next.js app can end up in a
# server log or, if misprefixed, in the browser bundle.

# Canonical origin — drives metadataBase, canonical tags, sitemap.xml and
# robots.txt. No trailing slash. Leave unset to use the production domain
# baked into src/lib/site.ts.
# PUBLIC by design: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.bhargavihealthworld.com

# The backend's origin. Read by BOTH the /api/contact proxy at request time and
# the content generator at build time.
#   Local:      http://localhost:3001
#   Production: the Railway URL, or the API subdomain once DNS is set
# Leave it UNSET and the build prints "Content generation skipped" and exits 0
# (D-016) — which is why a missing value is a silent no-op, not a build failure.
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Shared with the backend. Exempts this trusted server-side caller and the
# build from the public rate limit.
# 🔴 SERVER-ONLY. Never rename this to NEXT_PUBLIC_* — that would publish it to
# every visitor. It is read only inside a route handler and the build script,
# neither of which ships to the browser.
# BACKEND_API_KEY=

# --- Deliberately absent ----------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY      → backend only. The frontend never sends mail; it posts to
#                       /api/contact, and the backend notifies the clinic.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL    → 🔴 FORBIDDEN (decision D-034). Notification addresses are
#                       DATABASE ROWS (branches.notify_email, falling back to
#                       site_settings.default_notify_email) so the clinic can
#                       change them without a deploy. The backend's boot gate
#                       REFUSES TO START if this variable is set at all.
